R708=build('t_21d597c07ca4',708,'禪院','Chan monastery',['Chan cloister'],['Chan monastery','Zen monastery','Chan temple','Zen temple','Chan cloister','monastery of Chan'],'Seven independent title, colophon, memorial, and preface witnesses use the compound for the institution or named institutional residence.',O708,'A Chan monastery is the named residential institution in which an abbot presides and a recorded teaching career is located.','Lamp colophons identify Puming and Huirì Yunwen through the Chan monasteries where they serve as abbots. Transmission rosters attach named lineage figures to Baoing Chan Monastery, while collected-record contents organize successive bodies of sayings by Ciyun, Lianfeng, and Shousheng Chan Monasteries. A preface treats restoring Zhaojue Chan Monastery from overgrown ground as a major institutional act. The Chan bend is documentary and public: the monastery is not generic scenery but the named seat that locates a lineage figure, an abbacy, a body of sayings, and the restoration or transmission of the lineage.','The institutional name anchors named lineage figures, abbacies, recorded sayings, and lineage succession to public places.','The compound names an institution; it does not by itself prove the doctrinal affiliation of every person or building mentioned near it.',['禪寺','寺','院','住持','方丈','堂頭和尚'],[],['work:X78n1556','work:X78n1553','work:T47n1998A','work:J29nB224','work:J37nB371','work:J28nB202','work:X69n1360'])

