R710=build('t_f66eb09413fb',710,'三十棒','thirty blows',['a sentence of thirty blows'],['thirty blows','thirty strokes','thirty staff blows','sentence of thirty blows','give thirty blows'],'Eight works attest the fixed count as an assigned, threatened, deserved, retrospectively imposed, or ironically remitted beating.',O710,'Thirty blows is a fixed counted beating assigned as a public verdict in Chan encounters and later comments.','The sentence can arrive before action: Kaixian says it is due before crossing the teaching-hall gate, Dahui quotes its being due before stepping onto a boat, and Baoning makes movement itself incur it. It can also be retrospective or directed upward: Xuedou assigns it before Huineng reaches Caoxi, Nanjian has thirty blows for the World-Honored One, and Fohri Xi refuses to spare even one blow from earlier commentators. “I let you off with thirty blows” makes the sentence itself a pointed form of leniency in Jian Shan and Qingxi. Zen bends a conventional counted beating into a reusable teaching-seat judgement whose recipient may be monk, commentator, patriarch, or buddha.','A counted corporal sentence becomes a portable public verdict, including paradoxical formulas in which thirty blows are what “letting off” means.','The phrase names the assigned blows, not a universal explanation of why each recipient deserves them; each surrounding exchange supplies the charge.',['棒','一棒','喫棒','痛棒','德山棒','放汝三十棒'],['Kaixian Zhi','Dahui Zonggao','Fohri Xi','Nanjian Wen','Jian Shan','Baoning Renyong','Qingxi Hongjin','Xuedou Chongxian'],['work:wudeng-quanshu','work:guzunsu-yulu','chan:zongjian-falin','work:X66n1296','work:X81n1568','work:X84n1583','work:wudeng-huiyuan','work:liandeng-huiyao'])
